  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we know that the magnetic field due to a infinite wire at a distance of d is given as&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>but there are two wires so that the net magnetic field is given as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>A</mi></math></p>",
